      "id": "claim_7083a2d67caa4aa2b49d742fcfab50cd",
      "statement": "Each Script owns a LuaWrapper and its own Lua state. Script::start calls main and sets the state to Running; Script::update invokes Lua update only when that function exists, and stop marks the state Stopped. ScriptEngine starts idle scripts, starts added scripts immediately if it is already running, dispatches updates only to running scripts, and removes stopped scripts; stopping the engine pauses dispatch, and restarting it does not call main again for scripts still Running.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/scripting/elematelua/luawrapper.cpp#L12-L16",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6215472d54c62f6f759cc9ada0bc29055157866c1e0af01f7d450672cafd4b4f:"
